 "area": null,
 "description": "ALLOCENTRIC HELD-SURFACE MAP RECONSTRUCTION (block 203000). The map IS the held surface (180000) in WORLD coordinates: a first-class AlloCell{pose,value,density,residual,half_life,freshness,last_refresh_epoch,tier,stored,geom} on the game node, grown as the moving eye's SEEN observations are pose-registered into world coordinates. as_new MINTS a cell for a newly-seen world pose (unknown=ABSENCE, 161000 M3); as_blend EMA-ACCUMULATES the held value (freshness-weighted Kalman gain -- dwelt cells DENOISE/super-resolve as density climbs, changed cells ADOPT), climbs density, sets the integer surprise residual, and PROMOTES (refreshes the innovation clock); as_gate sets half_life INVERSELY by surprise (196000); as_freshness applies the integer-half-life decay law freshness=Ashr(c0,IDiv(now-last_refresh,half_life)) on the game's map_epoch clock; as_tier thresholds FRESH/GIST/LATENT; as_demote COARSENS the stored representation by Ashr with tier and NEVER deletes (198000 -- value preserved, so a revisit promotes back and recovers detail). The occupancy geom stays SEEN (depth-from-motion, 158000; walk frees authoritatively, 161000 merge). OFF by default: every rule guards on game.map_mode=='doom' AND an opt-in AlloParams{enabled=1} node the adapter creates only on opt-in -- absent it the 161000 map + every existing path are byte-identical. NO Rust, NO new Term (Ashr/IDiv/Abs/Max/IfThenElse/Gte/Lt/Plus/Times/Minus/Div/IndexAt/Exists/Not/And/Or/Eq exist).",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "doom_allocentric_surface",
  "description": "The map is the held surface in allocentric coordinates: pose-registered EMA accumulation with surprise-set integer-half-life decay and demotion -- a persistent, super-resolving, DECAYING reconstruction of the level from what the eye SEES as it moves."
 },
